4. Commercial Use

   (a) You may NOT make Commercial Use of any Covered Work that meets the
       Five Percent Threshold unless you first get Written Permission from
       the Licensor.

   (b) You MAY make Commercial Use of a Derivative Work that does NOT meet
       the Five Percent Threshold, as long as you follow Section 5
       (Credit) and every other term of this license.

   (c) Non-text files made by the Licensor (such as images, audio, or
       video), if any, may not be used commercially at all without Written
       Permission, no matter how much else you use.

   (d) "Written Permission" means a document, on paper or electronic, that
       is signed by the Licensor (an electronic signature counts), names
       you, and clearly grants Commercial Use. Nothing else counts as
       permission, including: silence, delay, not enforcing this license,
       accepting a donation or payment, merging your code, replying to a
       message, or any statement that is not signed. Written Permission
       covers only what it says, only for the party it names, and cannot
       be transferred unless it says so.

5. Credit (Attribution)

   Every Covered Work you share, publish, or run for others must:
     (a) keep this license file and the copyright notice above with the
         source code, unchanged;
     (b) show this notice where users can easily see it (for example, on
         an "About" or "Credits" screen, or the page footer):
         "Based on MoneyQuest by merrickfluellen
          (https://github.com/merrickfluellen), used under the MoneyQuest
          Source-Available License."; and
     (c) say clearly that you changed the work, if you did.
   You must not remove or hide any copyright or license notice, and you
   must not suggest that the Licensor made, supports, or endorses your work.

6. No Sublicensing; Passing It On

   You may not sublicense, sell, or transfer any rights under this license,
